    "summary" : "Blocking ambiguities in the requirement. Approve to accept the proposed defaults, or reject with feedback to answer them:\n- A1: Which service endpoints and what kind of abuse are in scope (e.g. request flooding, oversized payloads, brute-force attempts, duplicate submissions)? (proposed default: Apply per-client rate limiting to all public API endpoints and basic input size/validation limits; no authentication-specific or duplicate-submission protection.)\n- A2: What are the 'external checks' and what should happen when one is unavailable: reject the request (fail closed) or proceed without the check (fail open)? (proposed default: Treat every outbound call to a third-party system as an external check and fail closed: return HTTP 503 when the check cannot be completed.)\n",
